  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 12 - If
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_if
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: If
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "The <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>if</color></font>
    statement is used to make decisions based on conditions.\n\nFormat:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>if</color> (condition):</font>\n<indent=2em>code</indent>\n\nIf
    the condition is <color=#E57373>True</color>, the code inside will be executed. 
    \nIf it is <color=#E57373>False</color>, it will be skipped.\n\nExample:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>if</color> <color=#7FDFFF>condition</color>:</font>\n<indent=2em><font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55FF55>mine</color>()</font></indent>\n\nYou can also use conditions
    directly:\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>if</color> <color=#55FF55>scan</color>()
    <color=#7FDFFF>==</color> <color=#FF6EC7>\"WhiteOre\"</color>:</font>\n<indent=2em><font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55FF55>mine</color>()</font></indent>\n\nNote:\nIndentation is
    required.  \nAll code inside an <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#7FDFFF>if</color></font>
    statement must use the same indentation level."
  isImageBig: 0
